{"title":"2022 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The symbols, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009cf3eeb0ff3789cc057632947cadb200ab4663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b1352e2dc4380ca6efe5d978cb4bfa2745354e11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigcirc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> each represent a positive integer. Consider the following three equations.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cbf6917c53b1df2db0bd30de4c8f14c33e7e615.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle \\times \\triangle = 9\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/0030507ad50951303bfe8a21f8f195d4a727827d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\triangle + 5 = \\bigcirc\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df4dd6145a5fbba0a8f4a135d97cb5c90df1e08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\bigcirc \\times \\triangle = \\square\\]\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />\nWhat is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f126835463b8992ceb6449d6924cf33349e94e67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle \\times \\triangle = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, which occurs when either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3e8821aa8599b831a924fe22a294ef7e3a4f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/645b3f155dbe456892bb0811f821c6fe170e6ea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle = -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. However, because each symbol represents a positive integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3e8821aa8599b831a924fe22a294ef7e3a4f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. This means that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/c/e7c97d8f86b860021c11ab12e3c1b8cba60089a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5 = \\bigcirc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dcb749b9c956922283ad217fb3d1f3178c12770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigcirc \\times 3 = \\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>From the second equation, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3abde2d84ed7b80d7a5dd937399d08d3ef2cf35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigcirc = 3 + 5 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />. Thus:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b2bb501e82669c363252110a7dbb05c02be974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\times 3 = \\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e814836ed4dc9cfa91c9c9e64c1649eb2fb7271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square = \\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"69\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_TUC\" title=\"2022 CEMC TUC\">2022 CEMC TUC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_TUC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC TUC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_TUC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC TUC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay A Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Relay A Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Relay_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC TUC Problems/Relay B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Relay B Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_CEMC_TUC_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2022 CEMC TUC Problems/Problem 1 (page does not 